<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corazon Aquino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933–2009</span> · Also known as Cory Aquino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Corazon Aquino was president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1986 to 1992, the first woman to hold the office. The widow of the opposition leader Benigno Aquino Jr., murdered in 1983, she challenged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos">Ferdinand Marcos</a> in the 1986 snap election, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/people-power-revolution">People Power Revolution</a> drove Marcos into exile. Her government introduced the 1987 constitution and survived several coup attempts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corazon-aquino.jpg" alt="Corazon Aquino" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Airman Gerald B. Johnson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corazon_Aquino_1986.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
